_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 22
---
order: 22
---
short_label: VIII.22
---
statement: If three numbers are in continued proportion, and the first is square, then the third is also square.
---
proof:

Let *A, B,* and *C* be three numbers in continued proportion, and let *A* the first be square.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="220" height="140" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VIII.22 diagram" src="propVIII22.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VIII.22",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "B0;point;free;-1000,75;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;1000,75;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;-1000,110;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;1000,110;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,90,0;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black",
            "B1;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,30,0;0",
            "B2;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,120,0;0",
            "B;line;connect;B1,B2;black",
            "C1;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,30,0;0",
            "C2;point;proportion;A1,A2,B1,B2,B1,B2,C1,C3;0",
            "C;line;connect;C1,C2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that *C* the third is also square.

Since between *A* and *C* there is one mean proportional number, *B,* therefore *A* and *C* are similar plane numbers. But *A* is square, therefore *C* is also square. [!just VIII.20]

Therefore, *if three numbers are in continued proportion, and the first is square, then the third is also square.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

This proposition is used in a few propositions in this and the next book starting with @VIII.24.
